# 6. Current Ability and Potential Ability

Internally:

```text
CA = Current Ability
PA = Potential Ability
```

For example:

```text
Age: 17

CA: 68
PA: 156
```

But PA shouldn't guarantee development.

Development becomes something like:

$$
Development =
PotentialGap × Training × Coaching × Professionalism × PlayingTime × AgeFactor × Morale × RandomVariation
$$

Consequently:

Two players with PA 160 don't necessarily become equally good.

---

# 7. Dynamic potential

I'd actually improve on the traditional fixed-potential concept.

Instead of:

```text
PA = 160 forever
```

have:

```text
Base potential
Development ceiling
Development trajectory
```

Exceptional circumstances could alter trajectories slightly.

A 17-year-old getting regular first-team football might explode.

Another wonderkid could stagnate because of:

```text
poor professionalism
injuries
bad coaching
lack of playing time
poor morale
```

This produces emergent stories.

