# 15. Decision engine

Every player continuously evaluates possible actions.

Suppose a midfielder has:

```text
Pass
Dribble
Shoot
Hold ball
Cross
Recycle possession
```

Give each action a utility score:

$$
U(a) =
TechnicalAbility +
TacticalSuitability +
SpatialOpportunity +
PlayerMentality +
RiskPreference -
OppositionPressure
$$

Then introduce controlled randomness.

The highest utility action isn't automatically selected every time.

Otherwise matches become deterministic.

