# 70. Automated simulation testing

This is another way to beat badly vibe-coded games.

Have the computer simulate:

**100,000+ matches automatically.**

Then measure:

```text
Goals/match
Shots/match
Pass completion
Home advantage
Cards
Penalties
Possession
xG
Comebacks
Clean sheets
Player ratings
```

For example:

```text
100,000 MATCH TEST

Goals/match        2.68
Home win           43.1%
Draw               26.4%
Away win           30.5%

Shots/match        24.8
Pass accuracy      81.3%

Red cards          0.12
Penalties          0.27
```

Compare distributions with real football.

Then tune.

---

# 71. Long-term soak testing

The truly important test:

```text
SIMULATE 100 YEARS
```

automatically.

Then check:

```text
Did clubs go bankrupt?

Are transfer prices ridiculous?

Are there enough players?

Did player ability inflate?

Are wages exploding?

Are leagues competitive?

Are clubs building balanced squads?

Are goalkeepers disappearing?

Are old players retiring?

Are youth players developing?
```

This catches problems no ordinary unit test finds.

