# 77. Where you should try to BEAT Football Manager

Trying to have more raw content than [Football Manager](https://www.footballmanager.com/?utm_source=chatgpt.com) isn't realistic for an indie project.

Instead, pick **five areas where your simulation is exceptional**.

I'd choose:

### ① Dynamic football world

Leagues genuinely rise and fall in strength.

### ② Emergent history

Players, managers, clubs and rivalries create stories over decades.

### ③ Better long-term saves

Make 50–100-year careers a first-class feature instead of an edge case.

### ④ Modding

Expose almost everything through database/rule files.

### ⑤ African football

This could be your unique advantage.

Don't treat Africa as an afterthought.

Build:

```text
Nigeria
Ghana
South Africa
Egypt
Morocco
Tunisia
Algeria
Senegal
Ivory Coast
Cameroon
DR Congo
etc.
```

with continental football, youth development and dynamic league growth.

Imagine starting with a tiny Nigerian club in 2027 and playing until **2075**, gradually turning Nigeria into the world's strongest domestic league.

That is a compelling identity.

